'''Ararandewára''' is an extinct language formerly spoken on the [[Moju River (Acará)|Moju River]] in the state of [[Pará]], [[Brazil]].<ref>{{Cite book |last=Dellenbaugh |first=Frederick S. |url=http://archive.org/details/b2485587x |title=The lower Amazon : a narrative of explorations in the little known regions of the state of Pará, on the lower Amazon, with a record of archæological excavations on Marajó Island at the mouth of the Amazon River, and observations on the general resources of the county |date=1914 |publisher=New York; London : G.P. Putnam's Sons |others=Wellcome Library |pages=445–456}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |title=2013-010 {{!}} ISO 639-3 |url=https://iso639-3.sil.org/request/2013-010 |url-status=live |archive-url=http://web.archive.org/web/20190605172849/https://iso639-3.sil.org/request/2013-010 |archive-date=2019-06-05 |access-date=2026-01-26 |website=iso639-3.sil.org |language=en}}</ref>

